plete, nonfinite, substituted or wrong-budget members cannot supply a successful completed cohort. Predetermined original index0 must separately meet learning, unchanged quality, budget, device/provenance and physical serving/replay/admission conditions. No later best member substitutes for it.","classification":"Final exact held-out correct count must strictly exceed the authentic own-initial count and meet max(actual held-out majority count+1, exact uniform-binomial critical count). With1000 cases, critical counts remain136/24/16 for10/100/200 classes at alpha1/5000. This finite comparator does not reject every trivial predictor or arbitrary random network.","conditional_probability":"Only prospectively allocated all-five-null cohorts with iid uniform-per-example guesses within each member support the retained calculation: joint success is contained in a tail event<=1/5000; Markov gives P(atleast3)<=1/3000 without seed independence; at most30 allocated cohorts give a union bound<=0.01. This provides no unconditional/adaptive/repeated/score-selected attempt guarantee, no mixed-null, correlated/nonuniform/random-network guarantee and no regression, native-RL or population guarantee. Attempt-ledger completeness and remaining multiplicity are not independently audited here.","regression":"Finite positive scale, finite predictions/targets and positive held-out target variance remain mandatory. Exact binary64-rational SSE_final<SSE_initial and SSE_final<SST establish finite paired improvement and positive empirical held-out R-squared against the best constant for those exact targets. Existing standardized-RMSE arithmetic/ceilings, whole-five medians and served0 obligations remain unchanged; no population confidence follows.","historical_bars":"Exact historical/outcome-adaptive targets, slack and arithmetic retain their provenance. LeNet0.30, CIFAR1000.04 and Tiny0.008 chosen after observed0.012 are not promoted into independently justified published-model convergence by